18:**Preserve goals when correcting status.** Missing implementation or evidence does not retire or weaken an agreed product goal. Present the goal, the scoped current evidence, and the remaining work/acceptance criteria separately. Fingerprinting prevention, control of every disclosure and complete user-inspectable transaction history remain goals until explicitly changed by a product decision. A threat model defines how progress is tested; it must not silently narrow the goal. Preserve dated evidence and link unresolved work.
